      "owner": "@jeremi",
      "reason": "Debian classifies the Trixie issue as minor/no-DSA and has no Trixie fix. The v0.15.0 candidate rereview found that only the service binaries changed and every native closure dependency remained identical. Registry Notary still imports __isoc23_sscanf through the unchanged aws-lc dependency, whose reviewed call sites retain only fixed-format %lu and %lx conversions; neither exact candidate binary contains an effective vulnerable %mc format. Every file in both candidate executable closures remains digest-enforced because dynamic-symbol absence cannot truthfully express a format-string invariant.",
      "reviewed_at": "2026-07-28",
      "expires_at": "2026-08-28"
    },
